{"id": "1548926413179068487", "channel_id": "1545385622317965442", "author_id": "441633308217049088", "author_name": "salt9550", "content": "Today, I played the new season featuring the promised D-Effect Zone rework. As the development team explained, the difficulty of Hard has been significantly reduced, and many of the bosses that previously felt unreasonable have been removed. As a result, the overall difficulty does feel much more manageable than before.\nHowever, I still came away with a strong sense of dissatisfaction, and I think I can finally put into words why. No matter how this update is adjusted or justified, I do not think it can adequately answer one fundamental question: what advantage does the current system have over simply keeping the previous stages and adding Nightmare and Madness as Stages 6 and 7?\nThere was already a clear answer to this issue, and players had already experienced it for themselves. Stages that did not need to be removed were removed, and despite repeated requests to restore them, we have been told that restoring them is not possible, without a clear explanation as to why.\nFor players with lower overall account strength, the gap between each stage has become even larger than it was before. At the same time, even for highly invested players, much of the enjoyment that came from building and rotating a diverse set of ten different teams has been lost. Instead, the current structure strongly encourages players to concentrate their resources into five elite teams, which in my view has made the mode less enjoyable overall.\nI believe this underlying issue needs to be acknowledged. Otherwise, no matter how many additional balance adjustments or follow-up patches are made, it will be very difficult for the D-Effect Zone rework to fully address the concerns players have with the new structure.", "timestamp": "2026-09-14T05:20:34.563000+00:00", "thread_id": "1545385622317965442", "reactions": [{"emoji": "Celeste_agree", "emoji_id": "1400771815076528258", "count": 12}], "thread_title": "On the D-Effect Zone Adjustments", "forum_channel_id": "1184003940082262069"}
